Bombadil checks UI rules while it generates browser actions. Use this guide to compare rendered search results and check video-player consent.

Start with [property-based testing](/lore/property-based-testing). A property states a rule; generated actions search for a sequence that breaks it.
[Bombadil's introduction](https://github.com/antithesishq/bombadil/blob/832faf4d953e2c56d1d901aca1bb2c3c3170221d/docs/manual/src/01-introduction.md) describes that loop.

This is an optional tool, not a new rat-stack template dependency. The examples target Bombadil **0.7.10** and rat-stack at `60d73b434d6c62ac6a50eec2b4832003d1c01c9a`.

## Choose the test scope

Choose the scope that can observe the rule and control the failure.

| Tool | Use it for | Boundary |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Effect `it.prop` or `it.effect.prop` with `Arbitrary` | Domain laws over generated inputs | No browser rendering unless the harness includes it |
| Model tests over generated command sequences | Histories, retries and races; use barriers to force overlap | The model and adapter must represent the guarantees under test |
| Bombadil | Browser sequences, hydration and consent rules over captured UI state | No controlled server-side scheduling or proof of backend atomicity |

The table is a tool-selection guide. See the [events properties and models](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-stack/tree/60d73b434d6c62ac6a50eec2b4832003d1c01c9a/packages/events/test).
The [migration concurrency test](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-stack/blob/60d73b434d6c62ac6a50eec2b4832003d1c01c9a/apps/site/test/join-migration-concurrency.model.test.ts#L20-L64) uses explicit `Deferred` barriers.

Bombadil cannot establish whether a [Durable Object](/lore/workers-answer-requests-durable-objects-own-named-state) read-modify-write operation is race-free. A browser symptom is not a controlled server interleaving.
Use a server-side [model test](/lore/model-based-testing) for that race. Keep the browser test for the visible behavior.

## How the browser test works

Bombadil captures state, checks properties, picks an action, performs it, and waits for another capture.
An `extract` function reads browser state into a cell. A property reads the cell's `.current` value.

The [specification language](https://github.com/antithesishq/bombadil/blob/832faf4d953e2c56d1d901aca1bb2c3c3170221d/docs/manual/src/03-specification-language.md#formulas) uses linear temporal logic, or LTL:

- `always`: the condition holds in this state and every future state.
- `next`: it holds in the next state.
- `eventually`: it holds in this state or a future state.

These checks cover captured executions. A passing run is not an exhaustive proof.

[Weighted generators](https://github.com/antithesishq/bombadil/blob/832faf4d953e2c56d1d901aca1bb2c3c3170221d/docs/manual/src/03-specification-language.md#action-generators) give some actions more chances of selection.
For these examples, favor search submissions and matching play clicks alongside general navigation. Random navigation alone is not a coverage target.

Version 0.7.10 exports exactly four [browser default properties](https://github.com/antithesishq/bombadil/blob/832faf4d953e2c56d1d901aca1bb2c3c3170221d/lib/bombadil/src/specification/browser/defaults/properties.ts):

- No uncaught exceptions.
- No unhandled promise rejections.
- No console errors.
- Navigation response status below 400.

The HTTP property reads `PerformanceNavigationTiming.responseStatus`. It does not check every fetch, [RPC](/skills/learn-rat-stack), image or iframe response.
A swallowed RPC failure can pass that default. Add an observable UI rule when the defaults do not express the failure.

## Search count matches rendered rows

The teaching file keeps extractors and formulas only. Add action generators before using it as an exploration specification.

The search view [renders a count and a list](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-stack/blob/60d73b434d6c62ac6a50eec2b4832003d1c01c9a/apps/web/src/features/app.ts#L150-L179).
At this revision, the [handler](/systems/capabilities) [returns `total: matches.length`](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-stack/blob/60d73b434d6c62ac6a50eec2b4832003d1c01c9a/apps/site/src/capabilities/search.ts).

Compare those two DOM outputs after the Matches region settles:

```ts repo=rat-stack path=.brain/data/examples/bombadil-ui.spec.txt at=22a222c9eb3f08746c1ea7867b744cf81544ff5d lines=1-16 title="Count the rendered rows independently"

```

This property skips loading states and states without a count. It does not prove search relevance, freshness or eventual completion.
A paginated search would need a different count rule.

In one local run against rat-stack at `60d73b434d6c62ac6a50eec2b4832003d1c01c9a`, the planted bug displayed `result.total + 1`.
Bombadil reported **11 announced / 10 listed**. The shrunk trace retained **one Wait action**.
These are [local observations](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-stack/blob/22a222c9eb3f08746c1ea7867b744cf81544ff5d/.brain/data/examples/bombadil-ui-observations.json), not a detection-time guarantee.

## A player appears only after its own play click

The [/tube](/tube) view [chooses between a player and a play button](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-stack/blob/60d73b434d6c62ac6a50eec2b4832003d1c01c9a/apps/web/src/features/tube/index.ts#L37-L78).
Check the rendered iframe titles against action history, rather than reading the application's `playing` field.

First, collect player titles and the preceding click label. Normalize both action-label spellings:

```ts repo=rat-stack path=.brain/data/examples/bombadil-ui.spec.txt at=22a222c9eb3f08746c1ea7867b744cf81544ff5d lines=18-29 title="Read DOM output and the last action"

```

Then require an empty initial player list. Each new title must follow its own play click, unless it already existed in the same document:

```ts repo=rat-stack path=.brain/data/examples/bombadil-ui.spec.txt at=22a222c9eb3f08746c1ea7867b744cf81544ff5d lines=31-39 title="Check consent across captured states"

```

In one local run against rat-stack at `60d73b434d6c62ac6a50eec2b4832003d1c01c9a`, the planted bug replaced `isPlaying(model, video)` with `true`.
Bombadil reported **58 initial player iframes**, before any click. Shrinking retained **zero actions**.
After restoration and action-label normalization, a focused exercise recorded **137 iframe-bearing states with no violations**.
The [observation record](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-stack/blob/22a222c9eb3f08746c1ea7867b744cf81544ff5d/.brain/data/examples/bombadil-ui-observations.json) scopes those numbers to that local experiment.

This is a DOM-level privacy property. It cannot see network requests or an iframe inserted and removed between captures.
Thumbnails are outside its rule. Do not call it proof that no third-party request occurs before consent.

Both examples use independent observations: DOM count against DOM rows, or DOM players against action history.
Comparing a model field with itself is still a tautology when a fuzzer runs it.
[Tests that earn their place](/lore/tests-that-earn-their-place) explains why planted bugs matter.

## Vite friction and release drift

The same local experiment found these problems against `pnpm dev`. They are [observations at the tested revision](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-stack/blob/22a222c9eb3f08746c1ea7867b744cf81544ff5d/.brain/data/examples/bombadil-ui-observations.json), not general compatibility claims:

- Stock JavaScript instrumentation crashed inside a Vite-optimized chunk: `__bombadil__` was undefined. Runs needed `--instrument-javascript ''`, which disables that instrumentation.
- Click actions exposed `accessible_name` at runtime. The release's [TypeScript declaration](https://github.com/antithesishq/bombadil/blob/832faf4d953e2c56d1d901aca1bb2c3c3170221d/lib/bombadil/src/specification/browser/index.ts#L153-L171) says `accessibleName`. The extractor accepts both.
- Defaults mainly found development-server noise: local 404s for `/llms.txt`, `/openapi.json` and `/news.xml`, plus an HMR console error.

The docs also drifted. The [release workflow](https://github.com/antithesishq/bombadil/blob/832faf4d953e2c56d1d901aca1bb2c3c3170221d/docs/manual/src/04-workflows.md) uses output directories and `bombadil browser inspect`.
A [later main-branch workflow](https://github.com/antithesishq/bombadil/blob/69a61bc473f7ee01ceda024216ebc6921b7ea753/docs/manual/src/04-workflows.md) uses trace files and adds `bombadil trace`.
Read the release-tag manual and the installed command's help together.

Replay is best-effort. Shrinking searches for a shorter failing sequence and calibrates reproduction first.
A shorter trace is not necessarily minimal. Keep the original failure while you shrink it.

## Try it without changing the template

Recommendation: use an exact Bombadil version against an isolated **local production preview**, with signup and help delivery disabled.
Do not point random clicks at a deployed site: clicks can submit real forms. Keep the browser sandbox enabled.

1. Install exactly `@antithesishq/bombadil@0.7.10` in a separate experiment. Keep it out of the template's dependency graph.
2. Start the local production preview. Check that its local RPC path works and delivery stays off before exploration.
3. Export the two properties and add weighted generators that submit searches and click play buttons. Retain useful default properties.
4. Plant each bug separately. Require a failure, restore the code, then require a healthy run that exercises the rule.
5. Upload traces only on failure. Run shrinking outside the smoke-test budget, using the pinned release's workflow.

The production-preview variant was not measured in this experiment. Validate its wiring before treating it as coverage.

Next, use [model-based testing](/lore/model-based-testing) for server histories, or inspect the [RatTube player](/tube) to choose a browser rule.
